Date Functions in SQL

Date functions are used to manipulate and extract information from Date, Month, And Year values in SQL


1️⃣ YEAR()
Extracts the year from a date value.

SELECT YEAR(order_date) 
FROM orders_dimen;

2️⃣ MONTH()
Extracts the month (1–12) from a date value.

SELECT MONTH(order_date) 
FROM orders_dimen;

3️⃣ DAY()
Extracts the day (1–31) from a date value.

SELECT DAY(order_date) 
FROM orders_dimen;

EXAMPLE:

-- orders details for the orders which were placed in 2010
SELECT * FROM orders_dimen
WHERE YEAR(order_date)='2010';

-- Number of orders are placed in year of March 2010
SELECT * FROM orders_dimen
WHERE YEAR(order_date)='2010'
AND MONTH(order_date)='03';

-- order details of the orders which are placed in Jan, Mar, Oct of 2010
SELECT * FROM orders_dimen
WHERE YEAR(order_date)='2010'
AND MONTH(order_date) IN ('01','03','10');
